  "method": "Within each archived four-vCPU Micropod series, rank all clean rounds by bulk MiB/s. Take the bottom and top quarter and compute the median of each metric separately. Keep the two older full-Reno series separate from the peer holdout. They have distinct worker lifetimes. Use original client bytes and the VMM and supervisor PIDs in each fixture.",
  "scope": "Apple process counters cover setup and drain as well as the client byte interval. Instructions and cycles per byte use the payload counted in that byte interval. Mean host cores and runnable off-CPU thread-seconds per second use elapsed host counter time. The VMM process is a host accounting boundary. These figures cannot attribute work to individual vCPU threads, identify a guest kernel function, or separate host scheduling from offered CPU demand. Ranking by observed throughput makes these comparisons descriptive. The peer holdout contributes all 16 clean Micropod attempts, including the round in which the OrbStack peer had a fresh failure.",
